# What must not reach the build context. Two reasons, and the second is the important one:
# a smaller context is faster, but a context carrying bin/ and obj/ from a developer's machine
# produces an image built from artifacts nobody can reproduce — and one carrying .env or a local
# appsettings would bake a secret into a layer.

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/

.git/
.github/

# Generated output and local scratch, none of which the application needs to run.
contracts/
tools/node_modules/
publish/
TestResults/

# Local configuration and secrets. appsettings.json itself is deliberately not here: it holds the
# development defaults the startup guards refuse outside Development, and the published app expects
# it to exist.
.env
*.local.md
appsettings.*.local.json
